 ## Overview
-This method determines the global coordinates of an empty voxel position adjacent to a solid block that was hit by a raycast, enabling the placement of new blocks or mining operations. It solves the problem of translating a continuous raycast hit location into a discrete voxel grid coordinate while respecting the geometry of the hit face. It differs from its parent, [Voxel Block Interaction (Raycast Hit Detection)](3912-voxel-block-interaction-raycast-hit-detection.md), which only identifies the hit block; this method extends that result to find the specific neighbor slot for interaction.
+This method determines the empty voxel position adjacent to a hit solid block based on which face of the block was struck by a raycast [S2, unofficial]. It extends [Voxel Block Interaction (Raycast Hit Detection)](3912-voxel-block-interaction-raycast-hit-detection.md) by translating the continuous hit location into a discrete neighbor coordinate for block creation or retrieval [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs:**
-- `HitLocation`: The 3D world position where the raycast intersected the solid block.
-- `ChunkSizeX`, `ChunkSizeY`, `ChunkSizeZ`: The dimensions of a chunk in voxels.
-- `RaycastResults`: Data containing the hit location and potentially the hit block index (optional, as the method can derive the hit block from the location).
+- `HitLocation`: 3D world position of the raycast intersection [S2, unofficial].
+- `ChunkSizeX`, `ChunkSizeY`, `ChunkSizeZ`: Integer dimensions of a chunk in voxels, initialized from engine defaults [S2, unofficial].
+- `FindSolidBlock(HitLocation)`: Helper returning the chunk index and local block coordinates of the intersected solid block [S2, unofficial].
+- `GetBlock(ChunkX, ChunkY, LocalX, LocalY, LocalZ)`: Helper returning the material type at a voxel (0 for Air) [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
 
 **Outputs:**
-- `OutChunkIndex`: A 2D integer vector `(ChunkX, ChunkY)` identifying the chunk containing the target voxel.
-- `OutLocalBlock`: A 3D integer vector `(LocalX, LocalY, LocalZ)` identifying the voxel's position within that chunk.
-- `Success`: A boolean indicating if a valid, empty adjacent voxel was found.
+- `TargetChunkIndex`: 2D integer vector `(ChunkX, ChunkY)` identifying the chunk containing the target voxel [S2, unofficial].
+- `TargetLocalBlock`: 3D integer vector `(LocalX, LocalY, LocalZ)` identifying the voxel's position within that chunk [S2, unofficial].
+- `Success`: Boolean indicating if a valid, empty adjacent voxel was found [S2, unofficial].
 
 **Data Structures:**
-- `FIntPoint`: A 2D integer vector `(X, Y)`.
-- `FIntVector`: A 3D integer vector `(X, Y, Z)`.
-- `FVector`: A 3D floating-point vector `(X, Y, Z)`.
+- `FIntPoint`: 2D integer vector `(X, Y)` [S2, unofficial].
+- `FIntVector`: 3D integer vector `(X, Y, Z)` [S2, unofficial].
